This grant covers the contributors' localization work, not underlying game
artwork or other third-party material, whose rights remain with their owners.

3. Original game and patch distribution

"The Blues Brothers" (c) 1991 Titus Interactive. All rights in the original
game, its code and artwork remain with their respective owners. The project
and release patch do not distribute complete original game files and require
a legally obtained copy of the supported game edition. The patch contains
localization byte/pixel differences, project-authored scrolling code and
relocation changes, and the project-authored launcher; it is not limited to
translated text and pixels, nor is it a standalone copy of the game.

RUNME.COM, HARD.COM, INTRO.EXE, JOHN.SQZ, OH.SQZ and TERRY.SQZ in the supported
source edition originate from TDT/TRSI. Their inclusion in a user's source
copy or locally generated game directories does not relicense them under MIT
or CC BY 4.0. No license to redistribute the original game or TDT/TRSI
material is granted by this project.

4. Reference material

- cyxx/blues (https://github.com/cyxx/blues) was used only as a reference for
  understanding file formats. That repository had no license file when
  consulted; none of its code was copied. Project tools were written anew.
- Letter shapes for the large disk prompt and game-over text were rendered
  once from macOS system fonts (Superclarendon Black, Chalkboard SE Bold)
  into PNG masks in localization/pl/graphics/masks/. The patch does not
  contain font files.
- DOSBox-X (GPL-2.0) is used for testing and is not distributed in the patch.
